From: Prithwiraj Samanta <app@datainsights.ae>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 08:16:53 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 6/7] telecode: host postMessage hooks and stable board keys
 for the TeleDesign shell

When embedded (?project=<id>) the editor opens the project's canvas and
talks to its parent frame (same origin only): it posts
td-editor:ready/viewport/frames/selection/saved and handles
td-editor:open, :focus, :insert-frame (replying td-editor:frame-created),
:mark-board, :boards and :get-state.

HTML boards are frames registered in the project's boards.json. Node ids
cannot key that registry: a .fig import mints fresh ids from a
process-wide counter, so the same frame has a different id after every
reload. A board key is therefore stamped on the frame as shared plugin
data (telecode/board), which .fig persists, and resolved to the current
node at runtime. Three bridge commands (telecode_board_mark / _unmark /
_list) let the proxy manage those keys over the automation socket.
